WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.860
Good morning Hank. It's Tuesday.

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:06.380
Vidcon is this week. In a related story haaaaaaaaaaaaaaa is the sound that my anxiety makes

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.480
So Hank I'm in a hotel in Canada at a conference about educational video featuring like CGP Grey

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.500
and VSauce and MinutePhysics and Vi Hart, tons of fascinating people

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.740
But Hank the operative word there is 'Canada'!

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.600
Because as you remember from
the last time that we went to Canada

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:24.710
it is not easy for me to get into Canada.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.050
Right so this happens every time I come
to Canada, but I fly in I have my customs

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.230
forms filled out

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:34.160
I get in line and then I'm sent to 
like the Special Immigration office for

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.370
felons and other undesirables. And then I
am asked if I've ever been denied

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:41.239
entrance to Canada before and I say "yes"

00:00:41.239 --> 00:00:45.710
in 1995 I was denied entrance to your
fine country

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:49.760
due to insufficient funds. So Hank this was in the halcyon days before teenagers had

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.059
credit cards and when I was a freshman in
college a friend of mine and I, we drove

00:00:53.059 --> 00:00:54.969
up to Windsor, Ontario

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:58.719
is it 'friend of mine and I' or 'a friend of
mine and me'?

00:00:58.719 --> 00:01:02.949
a friend of mine and I; I was right
to begin with. I should

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:06.260
trust my instincts. So we drove to Windsor with a two liter bottle of Mountain Dew

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.729
a loaf of bread and some peanut butter

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:12.400
and fourteen dollars. I don't know by
what definition that constitutes

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.990
insufficient funds. So we try to cross
the border they search our car for

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:20.549
drugs then they turn us around for
insufficient funds, we go back to America

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:24.689
where they again search our car for
drugs, this time for three hours

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:28.900
even though we never got to Canada!
But it was fun we had a nice story when

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.980
we got back to college - we were too poor for Canada. And Hank I never had a problem getting into Canada

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:37.479
until 2001 when suddenly my name appeared on a list of undesirables.

00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:43.759
And now every single time I go to
Canada I am forced to explain again

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:46.320
that in 1995 I was deemed

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.799
insufficiently wealthy to visit this
great nation! Ohhhh and then they

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:53.320
search my bags and let me go on my way.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.219
So, anyway, today asked the guy is this
going to last forever? Is there any way I

00:01:56.219 --> 00:02:00.250
can clear my name? Make a donation to
your health care system or something

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:05.760
that will allow me to not be on the list? And he said, and I'm quoting him directly here Hank,

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:09.789
"Mister Green you're gonna die on that
list". So Hank that's my story of how I became

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:13.700
undesirable to Canadians. Canadians,
perhaps this helps you understand why I

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.099
don't tour here more often. Also Nerdfighters if history tells us anything it's

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:21.280
that Hank will fail to upload his video on Friday due
to VidCon stress.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.390
So prepare your punishment ideas and
leave them in comments.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:27.709
Did I say "comments" or "comets"? I really don't
ennunciate very well for an

00:02:27.709 --> 00:02:29.030
